# QDQC · Asset Usage

## Source of truth

- Raw sheets: `assert/image/*.png` (never edit / never delete).
- Manual slices: `assert/zip/*.zip` (Photoshop Save-for-Web cuts; never delete).
- App consumes copies under `web/public/` only.
- Registry: `web/src/data/assets.ts` maps id → path → chapter → role.

## Pipeline (`npm run sync:assets`)

1. Copy `assert/image` → `web/public/media/image` and music → `audio/`.
2. `crop-assets.mjs` — only NFC / posters / heroes **without** zip (`003`–`007`, `011`).
3. `process-zip-assets.py` — extract `assert/zip` → `media/slices/`, chroma-key cream/dark UI sheets, connectivity / column-split multi-component rows → `media/parts/`, rewrite matching `media/crops/*.webp` aliases.

Manual cuts may leave fringe: prefer transparent `parts/` sprites; for scene panels, slight CSS scale / soft mask is OK. Do not re-introduce fractional crops of multi-panel sheets.

## Image map

| Source | Role |
| --- | --- |
| `001`–`002` zip | Logo / brand mark tiles |
| `003`–`006` sheets | NFC card + character posters (crop script) |
| `007` `011` sheets | Desktop / ending heroes (crop script) |
| `008` zip | Butterfly hero + poses + flight / elements |
| `009` zip | Magpie hero + poses + flight / elements |
| `010` zip | Magpie bridge + day variants + icons |
| `012`–`18` zip | Storyboard / chapter panels |
| `19`–`22` zip | UI kit (desktop + mobile) |

Prefer `crops.*` and `parts.*` over full sheets in UI / R3F.

## Framing (do not over-crop)

- Never add decorative `transform: scale(1.02+)` on photos to hide seams — that chops more art.
- Narrative stills / banners / film strips: prefer `object-fit: contain`.
- Full-bleed heroes may use `cover` **without** extra scale; set `object-position` to protect faces / horizon / subject.
- Ultra-wide banners (`story-banner`, `story-quiet-tea`, `story-letter`, `story-coda`) must not be forced into tall portrait boxes via cover.
- When in doubt: show more of the illustration (letterbox) rather than crop.

